<% content_for :title, 'Staff privacy' %>
<div class="page-medium space-y-6">
  <%= page_header 'Staff privacy', subtitle: 'Rupert Staff connects to the Rupert instance chosen by your organization, which operates the service and controls staff accounts and employment records.' %>
  <section class="section-card">
    <%= section_heading 'Information used' %>
    <p class="text-sm">Your account email, staff record, clock times, time corrections, timesheet hours, pay records, time-off requests, notes, and review history are stored on that instance. Sign-in attempts record an IP address and device/browser information to protect accounts. Native app sessions include a device label and expiration date.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section-card">
    <%= section_heading 'Who can access it' %>
    <p class="text-sm">You can access your own staff member time records. Authorized managers and administrators can review timesheets and use approved hours for payroll. Rupert Staff does not include advertising or analytics SDKs or request access to your location, contacts, photos, camera, or microphone.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section-card">
    <%= section_heading 'Devices and retention' %>
    <p class="text-sm">The native app stores its sign-in token using the device's secure credential storage. Web sign-in uses the instance's browser session cookie. The web app does not cache timesheets for offline use. Employment and audit records stay on your organization's instance according to its retention policy.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section-card">
    <%= section_heading 'Your choices and support' %>
    <p class="text-sm">Sign out in the app, or revoke a native device session from Signed-in devices. Ask your organization's administrator to correct records, reset access, explain retention, or handle an account or data deletion request. Deleting the app does not delete employment records from the instance.</p>
  </section>
</div>
